1
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:06,050
[insects buzzing]

2
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:12,640
You,

3
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,560
you have always found me.

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,520
So please,

5
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:21,440
from now on, I'm asking you,

6
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,530
be the light again
that guides me.

7
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,530
[♪ opening music begins]

8
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,240
[♪ opening music ends]

9
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,120
Today at Omiyo Ohashi
Bridge, an incident

10
00:02:01,250 --> 00:02:02,830
occurred resulting
in a section-

11
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:03,960
What happened?

12
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,630
Guess the bridge is
out for the time being.

13
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:08,040
That's so scary!

14
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:11,210
Oh, I see.
So you saw Lisa?

15
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:15,300
[LARA] Lady Witch, why does
my big sister have legs?

16
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,140
Well, why else? It's because
she took my potion.

17
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,720
-But why?
-How should I know?

18
00:02:21,470 --> 00:02:23,640
She just took it from me
without even asking.

19
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:25,650
It was a real nuisance.

20
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:27,730
So you have an older sister?

21
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,270
[sighs]

22
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:34,400
I will not allow a mermaid
and a human to fall in love.

23
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:37,240
Why, big sis?

24
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:40,660
The fish swimming energetically

25
00:02:40,790 --> 00:02:42,660
above you here are
called sweetfish.

26
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,540
The fish swimming down at eye
level are carp and crucian carp.

27
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,630
Today I'd like to tell you about
the different kinds of fish

28
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:53,170
you can find in Lake Biwa.

29
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,170
[GIRL] Wow, so pretty!

30
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:59,350
-That there is a Biwa trout.
-You mean as in Lake Biwa?

31
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,140
You're right, that's
where it's from,

32
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:04,020
but someday it'll go back to
the river where it was born.

33
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,190
They're called anadromous fish.

34
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,520
That's right, very impressive.

35
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,400
[LISA] So?
[KOTA] It's a dead end.

36
00:03:14,070 --> 00:03:17,070
No matter where I searched, I
couldn't find anything special

37
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:18,660
Right.

38
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,870
It's been over 100 years
since the witch vanished,

39
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:23,120
so I think it's highly likely

40
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:25,250
that she's no longer
here at Lake Biwa.

41
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:28,170
How's your injury since then?

42
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,540
I'm fine.

43
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,710
It's just-—

44
00:03:36,130 --> 00:03:37,130
[gasps]

45
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:46,060
Lara, you have to understand.
We're running out of time.

46
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:50,980
[LARA] So you see, about that,
that was something

47
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:52,270
that Father gave to me.

48
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,480
1783 A.D.

49
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:55,150
And I was so happy.

50
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:57,240
Lara! Come on, hurry up!

51
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,160
[grunts]

52
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:05,330
[Lara giggles] I got him!

53
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:08,500
[cries out]

54
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:14,340
[LARA] I was so surprised.
His mouth is really huge.

55
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,170
Don't you think that's cute?

56
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:19,680
Hey, Lisa, you really like
that fish, don't you?

57
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,640
I mean, because you're
always together.

58
00:04:23,890 --> 00:04:25,350
Yeah, he's really funny.

59
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:28,140
No matter where I am,
he always finds me.

60
00:04:28,270 --> 00:04:29,350
He finds you?

61
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:33,020
He's a mysterious fish
with only his eyes

62
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:35,070
sticking out of the sand.

63
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:37,490
He once found a beautiful cave
filled with colorful minerals.

64
00:04:38,110 --> 00:04:39,530
He was able to find this

65
00:04:39,650 --> 00:04:41,280
very spot that we're
playing in today.

66
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,620
I reckon with that
light, he can find

67
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,700
anything in the world from
even the darkest corners.

68
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:50,790
Look! He found me again!

69
00:04:52,170 --> 00:04:53,250
[LARA] Oh!

70
00:04:54,330 --> 00:04:56,000
You're right, he found you!

71
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:57,670
[both giggle]

72
00:04:58,050 --> 00:04:59,170
Hey there!

73
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,260
Sorry for screaming.

74
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:09,350
[ROWAN] Lara was a truly
special princess to us all.

75
00:05:10,350 --> 00:05:14,560
However, after being betrayed
by those hideous humans, Lara-—

76
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,520
It can't be!

77
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,940
There is no longer
a princess who is

78
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:21,070
able to bring light
to this castle.

79
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,820
[ominous sound]

80
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:24,990
So the castle will
soon crumble.

81
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:29,450
We must abandon our
home and spend the rest

82
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,420
of our lives Searching
for somewhere new.

83
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,330
[GRACE] What a situation!

84
00:05:36,090 --> 00:05:37,550
[Lisa gasps]
[LARA] What?

85
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,880
It's her.

86
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,340
The witch.
It's Grace.

87
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:45,390
[GRACE] You pitiful
castle folk.

88
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:47,350
I do hope you're
not too distraught.

89
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:50,390
In place of that useless
king of yours, Rowan,

90
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:54,100
I myself will lead you to
new seas and a new home.

91
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,190
Follow me.

92
00:05:57,110 --> 00:05:58,770
Unless you want to
die, that is.

93
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:02,530
Where will you take us?

94
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,450
[GRACE] To the mansion
I built myself.

95
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,080
Why? Why would we go with you?

96
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,160
Because your king
asked me to take you.

97
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:14,080
If there's another safe
place you know of,

98
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:16,330
then please go right ahead.

99
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,710
[Grace laughs maniacally]

100
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:32,230
[Lisa screams]

101
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,140
[ocean waves fade]

102
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,730
[MAN] Look, it moved!

103
00:06:38,150 --> 00:06:39,150
It's alive!

104
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,150
[gasps]

105
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:43,650
[gasps]

106
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,450
[gasps]

107
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:48,160
[MAN] Is this real?

108
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:51,580
[pants]

109
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,450
[MAN] Oh, it's so creepy.

110
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,750
[LISA] Stay away!
[MAN] What's this?

111
00:06:59,170 --> 00:07:00,670
- Oh.
- No!

112
00:07:01,130 --> 00:07:02,210
Give it back!

113
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,340
[gasps]

114
00:07:06,090 --> 00:07:07,390
Let me go!

115
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:08,640
Help!

116
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,470
[screams]
[box shuts]

117
00:07:15,020 --> 00:07:17,060
[indistinct chatter]

118
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:21,480
Ladies and gentlemen, amazing
birds from faraway lands!

119
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:25,190
Give them a round of applause
for their lovely songs!

120
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,200
[audience applauds]

121
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:30,160
All right, next up,

122
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,540
prepare to meet a mythical
creature of the deep.

123
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:36,250
Now be careful not to be
deceived by her alluring eyes.

124
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:39,500
Ladies and gentlemen, I
present the mermaid!

125
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:41,040
[gasps]

126
00:07:42,090 --> 00:07:44,340
[♪ soft piano music]

127
00:07:47,130 --> 00:07:48,380
[gasps]

128
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:52,060
[audience applauds]

129
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:02,150
Let me out of here!
Let me out!

130
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:03,570
I need to get out of here!

131
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:05,150
Hey!

132
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:09,530
[gasps]

133
00:08:11,410 --> 00:08:14,490
[♪ soft piano music continues]

134
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:22,000
Ladies and gentlemen,
roll up and see for yourselves!

135
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:23,920
Proof that anything
is possible!

136
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:25,750
Truly the catch of the century!

137
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:28,380
Show your appreciation with
your cheers and money!

138
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:31,590
[♪ soft piano music continues]

139
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:37,180
[audience cheers]
The mermaid!

140
00:08:48,150 --> 00:08:49,280
Let me out.

141
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:53,780
I hate this place.

142
00:08:56,370 --> 00:08:59,120
It's so dark, I can't see.

143
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:10,420
[♪ tense music]

144
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,180
[♪ soft piano music]

145
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,180
[crowd screaming]

146
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:20,430
[gasping]

147
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,530
[low growling]

148
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:35,660
[grunting]

149
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,990
[intense growling]

150
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:46,000
[♪ piano music intensifies]

151
00:09:48,050 --> 00:09:49,210
[gasps]

152
00:09:50,970 --> 00:09:52,170
[♪ piano music ends]

153
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,260
[glass shattering]

154
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,100
Is it you?

155
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:07,230
You should know. After all,
I will always find you.

156
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:11,190
[♪ melancholic music]

157
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:17,120
Sorry I couldn't get there
right away to get you out.

158
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:19,200
What happened to you?

159
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,580
I took the witch's potion.

160
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,830
[Lisa gasps] Oh no.

161
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:29,550
[KOTA] As long as you're safe,
nothing else matters.

162
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,720
[LISA] Why go to such lengths?

163
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:36,140
You always used
to compliment me

164
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,180
on being
very good at finding you, Lisa.

165
00:10:38,510 --> 00:10:39,470
Remember?

166
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:44,520
Although it was you, you were
the one who found me first.

167
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:45,980
You saved me.

168
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:48,730
That made me happier
than anything else.

169
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,740
What will you do now?

170
00:10:57,410 --> 00:10:59,120
I know that my role ends here.

171
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,210
You should go back,
join everyone else.

172
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:08,590
Lady Lisa!

173
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:12,420
No, don't!
What are you doing?

174
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,300
Why?

175
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:22,470
You found me when I was alone
and lost in the darkness.

176
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,270
So in that case, from now on...

177
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:31,110
will you please be the
light that guides me?

178
00:11:33,070 --> 00:11:34,780
[♪ guitar strumming]

179
00:11:39,070 --> 00:11:41,200
- [KOTA] Lady Lisa!
-[LISA] I'm okay.

180
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,410
[KOTA] Have some potion.

181
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,630
Right, let's turn back today.

182
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:51,290
No, we'll keep going.

183
00:11:53,090 --> 00:11:55,470
To the place where Father
and the others went.

184
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,180
[LISA] Finally, we've made it.

185
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,180
1931 A.D. OKISHIMA

186
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:03,640
[underwater sounds]

187
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,230
Father!

188
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:12,400
[fast footsteps approaching]

189
00:12:14,020 --> 00:12:16,990
[ROWAN] Lisa, that... form.

190
00:12:18,450 --> 00:12:19,700
Why, my daughter?

191
00:12:20,530 --> 00:12:22,580
Why do you have
those hideous legs?

192
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:24,700
This place...

193
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,960
[ROWAN] This is the lair
of that accursed witch.

194
00:12:28,540 --> 00:12:30,250
After a long journey,

195
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:33,790
we arrived here having lost
almost all of our light.

196
00:12:36,170 --> 00:12:38,300
Now, Lisa, listen close.

197
00:12:40,010 --> 00:12:41,050
Just over there,

198
00:12:41,550 --> 00:12:43,220
Lara is sleeping.

199
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,680
- [LISA] Lara!
- She had turned to foam,

200
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:51,190
but I have bestowed light
upon her once more

201
00:12:52,190 --> 00:12:55,070
in the hope that
Lara might reclaim it.

202
00:12:56,070 --> 00:12:58,240
The light of the castle.

203
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:02,370
The light that only the
princess possesses

204
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:03,740
is what

205
00:13:04,830 --> 00:13:05,660
we need.

206
00:13:07,410 --> 00:13:10,290
I want to restore the
glory of my castle

207
00:13:11,210 --> 00:13:14,380
and my loving
family once again.

208
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:19,300
Lisa, in my absence, you must

209
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:22,720
wait for Lara's resurrection.

210
00:13:24,510 --> 00:13:25,640
Lady Lisa!

211
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,180
[gasps]

212
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:32,190
[LISA] The door, it won't open!

213
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:36,650
Humans are such
inconvenient creatures.

214
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:37,980
The witch!

215
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:43,030
How pathetic, the way they run
away as if scared by water.

216
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:45,120
Leave this place!

217
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,240
We will protect everybody here
until Lara eventually wakes up.

218
00:13:47,950 --> 00:13:49,120
Oh, do be quiet.

219
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:51,580
Rowan just wanted to
sleep like everyone else.

220
00:13:51,710 --> 00:13:53,170
You've deceived not only Lara,

221
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:54,960
but also my Father
and my family.

222
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,590
I won't dignify that
with an answer.

223
00:13:58,670 --> 00:14:01,550
Once my potion runs out,
you two will vanish into foam.

224
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:04,430
This is a sacred place.

225
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:07,300
Return to the surface, humans.

226
00:14:13,230 --> 00:14:14,810
KOTA MINASE

227
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:17,060
- [KOTA] Kota?
-That's what I've chosen.

228
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,230
That's your name from now on.

229
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:25,280
[KOTA] Okay. I will follow you
wherever you go.

230
00:14:26,370 --> 00:14:27,990
[LISA] Just as the witch said,

231
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,080
that potion
is about to run out.

232
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,910
So before we turn to
foam and vanish,

233
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:35,210
we have to get our
hands on that potion.

234
00:14:36,330 --> 00:14:39,290
And I will do anything
to make sure that happens.

235
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,590
SEIZO HORIKOSHI

236
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:42,800
KYOTO CHUO UNIVERSITY

237
00:14:43,630 --> 00:14:46,050
[MAN] Hmm, what's this?

238
00:14:47,010 --> 00:14:48,050
[LISA] This is...

239
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:51,560
something that will
change your life.

240
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:56,270
[magical sound]

241
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:58,440
To have to rely on the
hands of those despicable

242
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,730
humans is abhorrent.

243
00:15:00,570 --> 00:15:03,400
However, seeing as this
potion is forbidden for us

244
00:15:03,990 --> 00:15:05,990
and it must be
acceptable for humans,

245
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:08,280
it was a gamble worth taking.

246
00:15:08,580 --> 00:15:10,240
[magical sound]

247
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:13,330
[MAN] I was captivated by
the brilliant light that

248
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:15,460
this mysterious potion held.

249
00:15:16,370 --> 00:15:18,170
I have dreamed of
such a medicine

250
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:20,960
which unlocks infinite
possibilities for life.

251
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:23,590
[LISA] The structure
of human knowledge

252
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,050
differs vastly from that
of the mermaid world,

253
00:15:26,590 --> 00:15:28,890
hypothesis and verifications.

254
00:15:29,010 --> 00:15:32,100
However, the more we understood
it, the more we realized

255
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:34,770
that recreating the potion
would be no easy fit.

256
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,020
[MAN] It seemed to
contain life itself,

257
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:41,440
as though the Star of Life
dwelt within it.

258
00:15:42,190 --> 00:15:45,150
Days passed, and we continued
to pursue this special light.

259
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:46,780
[magic sound]

260
00:15:46,900 --> 00:15:49,200
It was as though it
were invisible to us.

261
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:52,330
[LISA] Just what is the
true nature of this light?

262
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:53,990
[MAN] I couldn't understand

263
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,040
where the light came from
in the first place.

264
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,000
I need to know...

265
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,210
I have to know the essence
of this radiant life.

266
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:04,340
However, it...

267
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:05,670
[BOTH] seems that-—

268
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:09,010
[LISA] I have unfortunately
run out of time.

269
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,640
HORIKOSHI FAMILY GRAVE

270
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:13,310
Human words are so
unnecessarily exaggerated,

271
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:16,180
embellishing their own
short lives like this.

272
00:16:16,310 --> 00:16:17,480
Such a waste of time.

273
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,480
[KOTA] He spent his entire
life creating this,

274
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:22,690
and all we have is
this poor imitation.

275
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:27,190
But regardless of that, even
though it's not the real thing,

276
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,450
it seems to delay
the process a little.

277
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,620
Yeah.

278
00:16:35,950 --> 00:16:38,620
1984 A.D.

279
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:41,250
[clock ticking]

280
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:49,130
THE NATURE OF LAKE BIWA
AND THE HISTORY OF ITS BIOLOGY

281
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,050
[clock keeps ticking]

282
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:53,140
VISITING PROFESSOR LISA SHIOMI

283
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,600
[clock keeps ticking]

284
00:17:05,110 --> 00:17:07,360
[LISA] Lara still hasn't
come back to life.

285
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:11,660
Even this fake potion is
beginning to lose its potency.

286
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:13,910
2026 A.D.

287
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:15,870
[KOTA] The survey of lake Biwa
will conclude very soon.

288
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,120
If I could find the witch,

289
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,450
the potion would surely-—

290
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:21,710
[both gasp]

291
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:25,340
Lady Lisa, you were right!

292
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,380
[LISA] Lara, please,
find it for us.

293
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:29,880
Find it soon.

294
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:33,680
[KOTA] Lady Lara's fine, but
she has human legs.

295
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:38,600
[LISA] Listen, Lara, a mermaid
and a human,

296
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:41,600
there's absolutely no way
they can love each other.

297
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:45,360
But... things might be
different tomorrow.

298
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:46,770
[gasps]

299
00:17:49,820 --> 00:17:52,950
Lara, that wonderful
light of yours,

300
00:17:53,910 --> 00:17:56,370
why won't you choose
to shine it on us?

301
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:03,250
AND NOW...

302
00:18:12,010 --> 00:18:13,050
[gasps]

303
00:18:27,230 --> 00:18:30,110
[breathing heavily]

304
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:32,610
[phone ringing]

305
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:34,700
LISA

306
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:39,410
[continues breathing heavily]

307
00:18:40,870 --> 00:18:41,700
[gasps]

308
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:45,120
[phone ringing]

309
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:50,380
[Lisa panting]

310
00:18:56,890 --> 00:18:59,220
[panting]

311
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:13,150
[gasps]

312
00:19:18,410 --> 00:19:19,450
[gasps]

313
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:22,540
[♪ melancholic piano music]

314
00:19:38,590 --> 00:19:40,510
[crying]

315
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,270
Lady Lisa!

316
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:54,690
[sighs]

317
00:19:58,070 --> 00:20:00,070
[Lisa grunts]

318
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,750
I know you must be
showing symptoms as well.

319
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,550
[sighs]

320
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,590
It won't be long until this
doesn't work anymore.

321
00:20:21,350 --> 00:20:23,260
[KOTA] But, if only...

322
00:20:24,350 --> 00:20:28,020
if only we had Lady
Lara's special power.

323
00:20:35,030 --> 00:20:37,400
[magical sound]

324
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,490
Lady Lisa?

325
00:20:39,610 --> 00:20:41,240
[magical sound]

326
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:47,040
[♪ fast flute music]

327
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,840
[gasps]

328
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:58,630
-[KOTA] Wasn't that...?
-[LISA] The witch.

329
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:00,720
No way!

330
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,600
She's been watching us
all along?

331
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,260
That's it, I found her.

332
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,230
She's been in the house.

333
00:21:08,890 --> 00:21:10,020
The whole time.

334
00:21:13,230 --> 00:21:15,270
[♪ closing music begins]

335
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,280
TRANSLATION:
SACHIKO TAKAHASHI

336
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,530
TIMING: ANDY ELLIS

337
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:23,070
EDITING AND TYPESETTING:
ASHLEY BARBOZA

338
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:25,370
QUALITY CONTROL:
RILEY DALTON

339
00:21:25,490 --> 00:21:27,790
TRANSLATION CHECK:
SRIRAM GURUNATHAN

340
00:22:40,150 --> 00:22:42,360
[♪ closing music ends]

341
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:44,530
[street noise]

342
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,570
One time, me and my brother got
into a fight.

343
00:22:48,030 --> 00:22:49,540
We didn't talk for a month.

344
00:22:50,580 --> 00:22:51,620
Hmm.

345
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:54,620
Hmm.

346
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:59,210
My big sister once said-—

347
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:00,670
[clatters]

348
00:23:02,340 --> 00:23:05,090
[♪ soft breeze and harp music]

349
00:23:09,140 --> 00:23:10,180
[gasps]

350
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:23,480
[♪ music intensifies]

351
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:27,160
[magical sound]

352
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:30,780
Ah!

353
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:39,540
[♪ orchestral music]

354
00:23:56,180 --> 00:23:57,100
[grunts]

355
00:23:57,350 --> 00:23:59,020
TO BE CONTINUED
